.SH NAME
Module::Build::Pluggable \- Module::Build meets plugins
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 5
\&    use Module::Build::Pluggable (
\&        \*(AqRepository\*(Aq,
\&        \*(AqReadmeMarkdownFromPod\*(Aq,
\&        \*(AqPPPort\*(Aq,
\&    );
\&
\&    my $builder = Module::Build::Pluggable\->new(
\&        ... # normal M::B args
\&    );
\&    $builder\->create_build_script();
.Ve
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
Module::Build::Pluggable adds pluggability for Module::Build.
.SH "HOW CAN I WRITE MY OWN PLUGIN?"
.IX Header "HOW CAN I WRITE MY OWN PLUGIN?"
Module::Build::Pluggable call \fBHOOK_prepare\fR on preparing arguments for \f(CW\*(C`Module::Build\->new\*(C'\fR, \fBHOOK_configure\fR on configuration step, and \fBHOOK_build\fR on build step.
.PP
That's all.
.PP
And if you want a help, you can use Module::Build::Pluggable::Base as base class.
